     EXPLANATION OF OPTION
 
     Use this option to modify or display the values for the logical 
     unit parameters.  Note that if you modify the logical unit size, 
     segment size, or the segment zero size, or are creating a logical 
     unit, the array controller automatically formats the logical 
     unit.  This means you must back up your data fileÄbyÄfile before 
     modifying a logical unit parameter.
 
     NOTE:  Procedures to modify and display the logical unit 
            parameters are included in the help screens following 
            the explanation of this option.
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
                                (CONTINUED)
     The "Modify/Display Logical Unit Parameters" option displays the 
     following information:
 
          Ä LUN Status
          Ä LUN Drives
          Ä Logical unit parameters
 
     NOTE:  See the help screens following the explanation of the 
            option for more information.
 
     The logical unit parameters include:
 
          Ä RAID level
          Ä Logical Block Size (bytes)
          Ä Logical Unit Size (mb)
          Ä Segment Size (blocks)
          Ä Segment Zero Size (blocks)
          Ä Delay Interval (tenth's of a second)
          Ä Blocks Per Delay Interval 
 
     NOTE:  See the help screens following the explanation of the 
            option for more information.
                                (CONTINUED)
     LUN STATUS:  A logical unit status describes the state of the 
     logical unit and the drives that comprise it.  The following 
     table gives a description of both the primary and secondary 
     status.  (Note that in the Array Configuration Editor, only the 
     primary statuses are displayed, and in sysadm, both the primary 
     and secondary statuses are displayed.)
 
